{"name":"Big Foot Feet","hex":"#e88e5a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"big","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Biangai."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of great size, large.","Fat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/big"},{"term":"foot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A biological structure found in many animals that is used for locomotion and that is frequently a separate organ at the terminal part of the leg.","Specifically, a human foot, which is found below the ankle and is used for standing and walking."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To use the foot to kick (usually a ball).","To pay (a bill)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foot"},{"term":"feet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of foot"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Fact; performance; feat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bigfoot","blocks":[{"text":"Bigfoot, or Sasquatch, is a large, hairy, mythical humanoid creature said to inhabit forests in North America, particularly in the Pacific Northwest. Bigfoot is featured in both American and Canadian folklore, and since the mid-20th century has become a cultural icon, permeating popular culture and becoming the subject of its own distinct subculture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Patterson_Gimlin_Bigfoot.jpg/330px-Patterson_Gimlin_Bigfoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bigfoot","wikidata":"Q44810"},{"title":"Foot","blocks":[{"text":"The foot is an anatomical structure found in many vertebrates. It is the terminal portion of a limb which bears weight and allows locomotion. In many animals with feet, the foot is an organ at the terminal part of the leg made up of one or more segments or bones, generally including claws and/or nails."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Foot_on_white_background.jpg/330px-Foot_on_white_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foot","wikidata":"Q15807"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/2016ShawneeBigfoot.jpg/500px-2016ShawneeBigfoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/2016ShawneeBigfoot.jpg/1280px-2016ShawneeBigfoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/2016ShawneeBigfoot.jpg/500px-2016ShawneeBigfoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Sassy the Sasquatch\" roadside attraction statue in the Garden of the Gods Wilderness within the Shawnee National Forest, Illinois[22]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2016ShawneeBigfoot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Pie_Grande.jpg/500px-Pie_Grande.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Pie_Grande.jpg/500px-Pie_Grande.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An artist's depiction of Bigfoot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APie_Grande.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Eureka_Humboldt_Times_04_September_1962.png/500px-Eureka_Humboldt_Times_04_September_1962.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Eureka_Humboldt_Times_04_September_1962.png/500px-Eureka_Humboldt_Times_04_September_1962.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photograph of an alleged Bigfoot footprint t